# Copy to docker/.env and edit. These are the only settings the container
# itself needs; everything about pr-daemon's behaviour stays in config.toml.
#
#   cp docker/.env.example docker/.env
#
# The three directories below can live anywhere. Keeping them beside this
# checkout is one tree to sync and is already gitignored (/.pr-daemon/):
#
#   PR_DAEMON_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/pr-daemon/.pr-daemon/config
#   PR_DAEMON_CREDENTIALS_DIR=/path/to/pr-daemon/.pr-daemon/credentials
#   PR_DAEMON_WORK=/path/to/pr-daemon/.pr-daemon/work
#
# Whatever you choose, keep the work directory out of the backup: docs/container.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- backed up
# Config: one directory holding config.toml. Small, and the status page writes it.
PR_DAEMON_CONFIG_DIR=/Users/you/.pr-daemon-config

# Credentials: the logins, mounted READ-ONLY.
#   claude-token              a `claude setup-token` token         (chmod 600)
#   gh-tokens/<owner>         one fine-grained GitHub PAT per repo owner (chmod 600)
#   gh-token                  fallback for owners without their own
#   cloudflare-token          only with [preview] dns = "cloudflare"
#   secrets/<org>__<repo>.env a repo's dev API keys, read by its own `up`
# docs/credentials.md lists the exact scopes each one needs.
PR_DAEMON_CREDENTIALS_DIR=/Users/you/.pr-daemon-credentials

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- not backed up
# The work disk: clones, worktrees, agent logs, screenshots, the database.
# Gigabytes, and all of it rebuildable from GitHub.
#
# IMPORTANT: this path is used on BOTH sides of the mount, so it must be a path
# that exists on the host and is allowed to be shared with Docker. A preview
# stack's `docker compose` runs against the host's Docker daemon and bind-mounts
# its worktree by host path, so the path has to mean the same thing in both
# places. Do not change it to a different container path.
PR_DAEMON_WORK=/Volumes/work/pr-daemon

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the rest
# The status page's port, published on the host's loopback only. It must be the
# same as `port` in config.toml — compose publishes this one, the page listens
# on that one. `just container-doctor` says so if they drift apart.
PR_DAEMON_PORT=7377

# Who the commits are by. Leave empty and pr-daemon uses the gh user it acts as
# with that account's noreply address.
PR_DAEMON_GIT_NAME=
PR_DAEMON_GIT_EMAIL=

# The host's Docker socket. A socket proxy goes here instead if you use one
# (docs/container.md, "The Docker socket").
DOCKER_SOCKET=/var/run/docker.sock

# Build options. Chromium (for a PR's screenshots) is about 400 MB.
PR_DAEMON_PLAYWRIGHT=true
# Extra Debian packages your repositories need, space separated.
PR_DAEMON_EXTRA_APT=
# Anything else they need: one shell command line, run as root during the build.
# `just container-doctor` cannot tell you about these — a missing one shows up as
# a stack whose `up` fails, so check the list in your projects' justfiles. Pin the
# version. For example, the nhost CLI:
#   PR_DAEMON_EXTRA_SETUP=curl -fsSL https://github.com/nhost/nhost/releases/download/cli%401.53.0/cli-1.53.0-linux-arm64.tar.gz | tar -xz -C /usr/local/bin cli && mv /usr/local/bin/cli /usr/local/bin/nhost && nhost --version
PR_DAEMON_EXTRA_SETUP=

# Only if a project's `up` starts a plain dev server rather than containers:
# the port range to publish (and the commented `ports:` line in compose.yaml).
# docs/container.md, "If your stack isn't Docker".
PR_DAEMON_STACK_PORTS=30000-30031

# Limits
PR_DAEMON_PIDS_LIMIT=4096
PR_DAEMON_TMPFS_SIZE=2g
TZ=UTC
